# Build-context exclusions.
#
# The api image is PUBLISHED PUBLICLY (ghcr.io/valve-tech/explore-api), so the
# priority here is that no secret can reach a layer. packages/api/Dockerfile
# copies explicit paths today (never `COPY . .`), which is what keeps the
# gitignored root `.env` out of the image — this file is the defense-in-depth
# so that a future broader COPY can't silently leak it.
#
# Secondary benefit: a much smaller context upload per build.

# ── Secrets / local env — must never enter the context ──────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*

# ── VCS / CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ── Dependencies + build output (npm ci / npm run build regenerate these) ───
node_modules
**/node_modules
packages/*/dist
shared/dist

# ── Test + tooling artifacts (never needed to build the image) ──────────────
coverage
**/coverage
playwright-report
test-results
**/.vite
.claude

# ── Editor / OS noise ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea
*.log
